From 4a52ced4af250abedde79cba5bbebf0945922a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:48:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Eden (Doris): undo build 21's texture changes; report fences
 released before GPU-written data is copied back

- Build 21 marked textures created from GPU drawings as GPU-drawn, copied newer drawings between
  same-layout textures that Eden keeps apart, and brought textures up to date before the cleanup
  copied them back. Its log shows TotK recycling texture memory at arbitrary offsets: those
  copies moved one terrain tile's data into another, and a 320x180 RGBA8 drawing into a 320x180
  B10G11R11 texture every frame. The ground glitch was unchanged and grass vanished; all three
  are undone (the counters stay in the report).
- Report: fences signalled, how many were released to the game at once while bytes the GPU
  wrote into buffers before them were still to be copied back (GPU fence behaviour
  "Immediate"), and how much was copied back at fences. Pairs of textures kept apart are
  logged in full once per pair of shapes (the offsets vary as memory is reused).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
